  "version": 1,
  "_note": "Canonical routing surface for cook. raw_signal -> canonical tag -> routes_to. Seeded from every standards/*/_INDEX.md keyword column (the global shelf routes here, not via a keyword table), then extended with gap-closing synonyms. Within-domain ref selection still uses the domain _INDEX.md tables; this file drives top-level routing only. Verify parity with verify/done/check-vocab-parity.py, which skips any unrouted shelf and an allowlist of intentionally-generic tokens. The routes_to targets double as the public --flag namespace for /cook invocations: concern:<name> -> --<name> (loads one global ref), domain:<name> -> --<name> (loads full domain shelf) or --<name>:<ref> (loads single domain ref), shelf:global -> --global (loads full global shelf). Aliases match prose, extensions, frameworks and whole path segments (never part of a file name). A tag with match_name false does not match on its own name. Renaming or deleting a routes_to target is a breaking CLI change. The apple-shared tag holds vocabulary valid on both Apple platforms (SwiftUI, SwiftData, Keychain, ...); it lists domain:ios and domain:macos, and cook_cache.py classify narrows it to the platform the project declares, or routes nothing and sets platform_ambiguous.",
